is this  needs to change and so we would change  like go for it let's do it i love that  what did you want to add when you were  changing those lines this process was  different because we worked on  everything um we were always script  buddies  yeah also depending on what we shot and  how it went and if anything was  improvised or if we didn't get something  or we got extra whatever it was then we  would adjust further the following  scenes so that it would make more sense  or call back to a joke that was made  that wasn't previously in the script so  just like constantly updating so that it  was like a real cohesive story yeah was  that fun for you i would imagine that's  not always the case that you can work  and change up the script so much usually  people get  are annoyed with me because i want to do  that so i guess and i'm so grateful  i really am  i guess now because because it's my  movie it's you know  because i was a producer yeah that  nobody could tell me i couldn't do that  right even if you weren't a producer i  would have not been annoyed  like some people really do get annoyed  they're like you're just an actress how  could you know but like i have a brain  in my head  yeah  but yeah no cooper was super  collaborative and especially in that way  he  like me has the ability to learn lines  pretty quickly so we could rewrite a  whole scene beforehand and then wow and  then shoot it the characters in this  movie they do face the dilemma of  figuring out their futures what they're  going to do and we were curious if  either of you was not in acting have you  ever thought about what another future  could be like for you if you'd made a  big change at a younger age i think i'd  be a florist i always wanted to have  like a tiny little flower shop that also  made like the best cookie and the best  cup of coffee just it's like one stop  shop  in the morning when you're like going to  apologize to somebody  that's i love that story apology flower  that's what